      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good question!\n\n`descriptorImageInfos` is defined outside of this loop, and `push_back` adds one new default-initialized value and returns it by reference but you\u0027re correct in that subsequent push_back calls technically invalidate that reference. But getting the address of the reference should still be pointing to the same spot...\n\nTo be safer, perhaps I could do `writeInfo.pImageInfo \u003d descriptorImageInfos.end();`? then the next call, when another is pushed back, end() will be pointing to the subsequent entry? \nLMKWYT!",
